cryptic_sort
============

Write a function:

    def cryptic_sort(strings: list[str]) -> list

Sort a list of strings using three tie-breaking keys, in this order:
  1. By LENGTH (shorter first).
  2. Then by LOWERCASE alphabetical order.
  3. Then by NUMBER OF VOWELS (a, e, i, o, u — both cases).

Examples:
    cryptic_sort(["bb", "a", "cc"])         -> ["a", "bb", "cc"]
    cryptic_sort(["cat", "dog", "ant"])     -> ["ant", "cat", "dog"]
    cryptic_sort(["hello", "Hi", "hey"])    -> ["Hi", "hey", "hello"]
